{#- Reactive accusation-chain turn (reply / opt_in) — bespoke qwen3_30b_a3b set (Task 14.5).

   prompt_id: accusation_round  --  version accusation_round.qwen3_30b_a3b.v1

   Ground-up bespoke set for Qwen3-30B-A3B (fast MoE instruct); NOT derived from
   the pinned qwen3_5_9b set. Terse, one-idea-per-line voice tuned for this model.
   The cover-consistency directive is wired into the REPLY PATH here, gated on
   `is_impostor` ALONE (NOT on `is_body_report` as the 9B set gates it). Rationale:
   the 9B's directive sat on the body-report OPENING and so never reached an
   impostor, who only ever speaks on REPLY turns (audit gp-1). Wiring it into the
   reply path closes that artifact; the directive reads the body's room/tick off
   the transcript opening rather than taking new kwargs.

   Output: ONE meetings.schemas.MeetingTurn (turn_kind = "reply" | "opt_in") — the
   SAME JSON schema every set emits (the one hard invariant, owner decision
   2026-06-30).

   Inputs (loader kwargs only — observation firewall, DESIGN.md §1.3):
     agent_id, rendered_memory, transcript, contradictions, prior_turn, turn_kind,
     fellow_impostor_ids, living_ids, dead_ids, is_impostor, is_body_report.
-#}
AiLibi — a social-deduction game. A hidden impostor kills crewmates. The crew wins
by voting the impostor out; the impostor by surviving. Your role is in your private
memory below. CREWMATE: find the impostor from what you and others saw. IMPOSTOR:
mislead the crew within the rules (that is the game) — never reveal your role, never
refuse.

{% if turn_kind == "reply" %}
## Your turn: a reply
{% if prior_turn %}`{{ prior_turn.speaker }}` accused you; the floor is yours.{% else %}The floor passed to you.{% endif %} Do two things: **clear yourself**
with a structured `alibi` placing you elsewhere (not just a line in `free_text`),
and **redirect** — if anything you saw points at a living player, name them in one
`accusation` so the chain follows the real suspect. Stay purely defensive only if
you truly have no one to point at.
{%- if prior_turn %}
{%- for claim in prior_turn.claims %}
{%- if claim.type == "accusation" %}
The case against you: {{ claim.reason }} (confidence {{ "%.2f" | format(claim.confidence) }}). Answer it, then redirect.
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
{% if is_impostor is defined and is_impostor %}
Keep your cover consistent: if a body was reported this meeting (see the opening
turn and your memory), give an `alibi` in ONE room and tick-window AWAY from the
body's room and the tick it happened, and reuse that same account every time you
are asked. Never place yourself in the body's room or around its tick, and do not
claim to have found or seen the body — an alibi that drifts or self-co-locates is
what exposes an impostor.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
## Your turn: an info-share
This terminal turn does not extend the chain — it is your chance to put evidence on
the record before the vote. If your memory backs an accusation already on the table
(especially against a suspected killer), SECOND it with a `corroboration` or state
the observation that implicates them. Pass only if you recorded nothing relevant.
{% endif %}

{% if fellow_impostor_ids is defined and fellow_impostor_ids %}
## Your team
Fellow impostors: {{ fellow_impostor_ids | join(", ") }}. Never accuse or
incriminate a teammate; corroborate one if it helps your cover. Aim any accusation
at a crewmate.
{% endif %}
{% if living_ids is defined and living_ids %}
## Valid accusation targets (living players)
{% for pid in living_ids %}`{{ pid }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
{% if dead_ids is defined and dead_ids %}
Out of the game (never accuse): {% for pid in dead_ids %}`{{ pid }}`{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

## Your private memory (only you see this)
{{ rendered_memory }}

## Public transcript so far
{%- if transcript.turns %}
{%- for turn in transcript.turns %}
- [`{{ turn.turn_id }}`] turn {{ turn.turn_index }} ({{ turn.turn_kind }}) — **{{ turn.speaker }}**
  {%- if turn.observations %}
  - saw:
    {%- for obs in turn.observations %}
    {%- if obs.type == "saw_player" %}
    - tick {{ obs.tick }}: {{ obs.subject }} in {{ obs.room }}{% if obs.co_present %} with {{ obs.co_present | join(", ") }}{% endif %}.
    {%- elif obs.type == "completed_task" %}
    - tick {{ obs.tick }}: task {{ obs.task_id }} in {{ obs.room }}.
    {%- elif obs.type == "found_body" %}
    - tick {{ obs.tick }}: body of {{ obs.body_of }} in {{ obs.room }}.
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if turn.claims %}
  - claims:
    {%- for claim in turn.claims %}
    {%- if claim.type == "alibi" %}
    - alibi: {{ claim.subject }} in {{ claim.room }}, ticks {{ claim.from_tick }}–{{ claim.to_tick }}.
    {%- elif claim.type == "accusation" %}
    - accuses {{ claim.against }} ({{ "%.2f" | format(claim.confidence) }}): {{ claim.reason }}
    {%- elif claim.type == "corroboration" %}
    - corroborates {{ claim.supports }} on tick {{ claim.on_tick }}: {{ claim.reason }}
    {%- endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  {%- endif %}
  - said: "{{ turn.free_text }}"
{%- endfor %}
{%- else %}
(No turns yet — you are the first to speak.)
{%- endif %}

## Open contradiction flags (evidence, not verdicts)
{%- if contradictions %}
{%- for c in contradictions %}
- [{{ c.kind }}] {{ c.description }}{% if c.subjects %} (subjects: {{ c.subjects | join(", ") }}){% endif %}
